+# Embedded itijah provenance
+
+Source: DiaaEddin/itijah tag v0.2.1, fetched as
+https://codeload.github.com/DiaaEddin/itijah/tar.gz/refs/tags/v0.2.1
+Archive SHA-256: b885878fe9edf5a2b2b2fc270aa74cfa498eeafd1a2fc60cdb4aa275d3047093
+
+The original upstream manifest declares version 0.2.1 and minimum Zig 0.15.2.
+The embedded manifest requires Zig 0.16.0 and omits the unused upstream UCD
+and uucode dependency entries. Conformance data is downloaded separately
+with pinned SHA-256 checksums; runtime Unicode tables come from Ghostty.
+The embedded build adapter omits the optional benchmark graph, which uses
+pre-0.16 filesystem APIs. Ghostty constructs the module for each target
+and supplies its existing singleton uucode module and generated tables.
+The upstream bidirectional implementation is preserved. The conformance test
+mode is fixed to the full suite instead of reading environment variables
+through the pre-0.16 process API. Arabic glyph
+shaping is performed by CoreText or HarfBuzz, not itijah's shaping stubs.
+
+The Ghostty port derives from PR #11079 at
+0d4ba38f86dea76784d7e7c3760202a1e67c8118. Paragraph first-strong direction
+uses auto_ltr, the applicable change from PR #13563 at
+39122a5a58460858ae6dc0b17178e797214ae6ec.
+Rendering and conformance validation remain required; this provenance file
+is not evidence that those tests have passed.
+
+Array-list initialization uses Zig 0.16 `.empty` instead of the upstream
+0.15 defaults and empty struct literals.
